<resources>

    <!--
      THE SECOND SPLASH LIVES HERE.

      From Android 12, every app that targets API 31+ gets a splash screen from the PLATFORM,
      before a single frame of the app runs. It draws the launcher icon on a coloured window —
      so once the launcher icon became the HUMBEE mark, the app showed the mark, then showed
      `src/views/splash/SplashScreen.tsx` with the mark AND the tagline. Two splashes, and the
      first one was never written by anyone.

      It cannot be switched off — `SplashScreen.setKeepOnScreenCondition` only makes it last
      LONGER, and there is no attribute that skips it. What it can be is empty: a white window
      with a transparent icon, indistinguishable from the white the JS splash sits on. The
      hand-off then reads as one screen that simply takes a moment to draw its logo.

      Keep this in step with `AppThemeBase` — the splash attributes are the only difference.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="AppThemeBase">
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/humbee_surface</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon_none</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
    </style>

</resources>
